  "comment": "The approved app list. An account on 'Approved apps only' (the default) may install and run these and nothing else; an account opened to the whole store may have anything on Flathub that is not blocked for it, and an approval also overrides the computer's content ceiling for that one app. kosherd installs, from upstream Flathub. An admin adds to or removes from this list in KosherOS Admin; this is the starting shelf, chosen so an ordinary family, a student and a developer all find what they need on day one without anybody curating a list. Each entry carries the freedesktop categories the Store shelves it by. An entry whose ref is nixpkgs#<package> comes from upstream nixpkgs instead and is installed into the asking account's own Nix profile; that is how the AI coding tools and the editors that have no Flatpak are here. An entry whose ref is upstream#<name> is the developer's own signed build, for an app whose Nix build cannot find the computer's graphics drivers (kosherd/upstreamapps.py); it too goes into the asking account's own home. Later portal-managed.",
